  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-11-26T14:22:47.163Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently, the JSON implementation internally always parses as a double. However, most modern JSON implementations implicitly read numbers that don't have decimals as integers instead of floats by default, converting only if required.\n\nIt would be amazing if we could explicitly request a number to be fetched as an int, instead of as a double, without losing precision. Something like .TryGetInt() or something.\n\nThis could also be implemented on number by flooring - but flooring in all cases here would reduce accuracy when working with large numbers.\n\nThis is especially useful for currency-like values, such as livestream donations.",
